## POST-RUN AMENDMENT (2026-08-15, after results existed)
Three code changes were made AFTER the freeze above. None altered the definition
of any statistic, and none was made while an outcome number was visible.

D1  severity_collect.py — G0.9 originally scanned this file's own source and
    self-matched on its FORBIDDEN_COLUMNS declaration, so the first run aborted.
    Rewritten to scan the SQL actually executed (RecordingConnection): a strictly
    stronger check. Made before any label or result file existed.
D2  severity_analyze.py — _decompose now accepts precomputed wg_tot/wg_b1 so the
    bootstrap hoists two outcome-independent bincounts out of the outcome loop.
    Mathematically identical; covered by test_integer_weights_equal_row_replication
    and test_mixture_identity_holds. Made after labels existed but before any
    outcome number was computed (only G0.1/G0.2/label-agreement had been printed).
D3  severity_analyze.py — component (DVSA section) labels were omitted from the
    bootstrap, so they would have carried no CI, which the brief requires. Added to
    the same shared resample. Same timing as D2.

Deviation recorded in the prereg body §3 (fail-gated n_dangerous) stands unchanged.

